    "text": "Those soldiers were sent into an impossible situation for a political stunt. The weather in the Eastern Med from March to June consists of stormy seas, 40-50kt Southerly winds. Also, the currents run South to North. The pier should have been protected by a breakwater. It wasn't. It was subjected to lateral stresses of wind and sea against which no degree of anchoring can protect. We don't have the spare redundant merchant hulls to sink as a breakwater. Those soldiers were facing a natural threat from the climate and a terrorist threat from land. They made a herculean effort for that pier to operate for 3 out of its 33 days there. Typical Biden-style operation - ill-informed, ill-considered and dangerous for the troops involved with little possibility of success.",
